/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1905177901.arc-codegen-similar/9/codegen_prompts/3.md:327:- A background grid has four panels separated by three full-height separator columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1905177901.arc-codegen-similar/9/codegen_prompts/3.md:328:- The first two panels contain same-size binary masks; the last two contain solid same-size color squares.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1905177901.arc-codegen-similar/9/codegen_prompts/3.md:329:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1905177901.arc-codegen-similar/9/codegen_prompts/3.md:330:- Use the second mask as an outer layout. For each foreground cell in that outer mask, place a tile equal to the first mask, coloring its foreground with the first solid-square color and its background with the second solid-square color; outer background cells become all second solid-square color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1905177901.arc-codegen-similar/9/codegen_prompts/3.md:331:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1905177901.arc-codegen-similar/9/codegen_prompts/3.md:332:- The output is the Kronecker product of the two binary masks, with the two right-hand panel colors providing the palette.
